	w3m: WWW wo Miru Tool  version 0.5.3
		(C) Copyright Akinori ITO
			      Hironori SAKAMOTO
			      Fumitoshi UKAI

1. Introduction

     w3m is a pager with WWW capability. It IS a pager, but it can be
used as a text-mode WWW browser.

     The features of w3m are as follows:

* When reading an HTML document, you can follow links and view images
  (using an external image viewer).
* It has 'internet message mode', which determines the type of a
  document from its headers. If the Content-Type: field of the document
  is text/html, that document is displayed as an HTML document.
* You can turn URL-like strings such as 'http://example.net' in plain
  text into links to that URL.
* Scripts embedded in pages are executed by an embedded QuickJS engine
  (see "Recent changes" below).

w3m runs on modern Unix systems: Linux, the BSDs, macOS, and (via
Cygwin) Windows — see README.cygwin.

2. Recent changes (this fork)

* JavaScript support: an embedded QuickJS engine executes page scripts
  while loading, so pages that build their content with JavaScript now
  render. Heavy single-page apps still need a real browser; see the
  next item.
* External JavaScript renderer: the JS_RELOAD command (bound to X) pipes
  the current page through an external headless browser and swaps the
  rendered result in. Configure it with the "js_renderer" siteconf
  option or the shipped js-renderer helper script; see
  README.siteconf.
* Browser-style history: H moves to the previous page and L to the next
  page without closing the current buffer.
* Vim-like movement in the default keymap: b/e/w word motions, W/B/E
  big-word motions, C-d/C-u half page, C-f/C-b full page, 0 to the
  beginning of the line. The lynx keymap is unchanged.

3. Installation

Follow these instructions to install w3m.

 - You need the Boehm GC library. On Debian/Ubuntu, install the build
   dependencies:

	# apt install build-essential libgc-dev libgpm-dev \
		libssl-dev libimlib2-dev gettext

   libssl-dev is required for https; without it configure silently
   disables SSL and https:// URLs will fail. The other libraries are
   optional (GPM mouse support, inline images, translations).

 - Run configure.
   % ./configure

 - do make
   % make

 - do make install
   # make install

Windows: to compile w3m on MS-Windows, use Cygwin with the development
tools. Read README.cygwin for details.

